# Tests

Use `flutter_test`, `bloc_test`, and `mocktail`. Mirror `lib/` under `test/`.

```
lib/news/view/bloc/news_bloc.dart
test/news/view/news_bloc_test.dart
```

Run `fvm flutter test test/news/view/news_bloc_test.dart` from the repo root.

```dart
blocTest<NewsBloc, NewsState>(
  'loads headlines for the source',
  build: () => NewsBloc(loadNewsUC, watchFavoritesUC),
  act: (bloc) => bloc.init('bbc-news'),
  expect: () => [
    const NewsState.loading(),
    isA<NewsLoadedState>(),
  ],
);
```

- Test names describe behavior
- Mocks are private: `class _LoadNewsUCMock extends Mock implements LoadNewsUC {}`
- `setUp` builds the bloc; `tearDown` calls `bloc.close()`
- Cover the success path and the failure or empty path the bloc actually emits
- Widget tests wrap with `MaterialApp`. Pump past `configureDependencies` only when the widget resolves `get<T>()`
